Instance configurations for timberfs's template units live in this directory.

Each <instance>.conf defines the environment for one timberfs mount:

    BACKING=/var/log/timberfs-backing/applogs
    MOUNTPOINT=/var/log/apps
    EXTRA_OPTS=--allow-other

Then: systemctl enable --now timberfs@<instance>

Each otlp-<instance>.conf defines one OTLP shipper — a store, and the
OTLP/HTTP receiver its entries are posted to:

    STORE=/var/log/timberfs-backing/applogs/app.log
    ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4318
    EXTRA_OPTS=--service applogs

Then: systemctl enable --now timberfs-otlp@<instance>

Only these two units read a file from this directory. The rest are
configured with a systemd drop-in instead — the templated log intake
(systemctl edit timberfs-log@<instance>.service) and the two network
intakes, which are not templated because one listener serves every stream
(systemctl edit timberfs-forward.service, timberfs-otlp.service).

forests.d/*.conf lists the directories searched when a command is given a
bare handle instead of a path (see FORESTS in man 1 timberfs).

Commented examples: /usr/share/doc/timberfs/examples/
Manuals: man 1 timberfs, man 1 timber-otlp
